","type":"application/javascript","module-type":"library"},"$:/plugins/samsmith/codemirror6/readme":{"title":"$:/plugins/samsmith/codemirror6/readme","text":"! CodeMirror 6 editor

Replaces TiddlyWiki's default plain-textarea tiddler editor with [[CodeMirror 6|https://codemirror.net/]], across every tiddler type: wikitext, JavaScript, CSS, HTML, JSON, Markdown, and plain text.

!! Features

* Syntax highlighting, matched to each tiddler's content type (with a purpose-built highlighter for TiddlyWiki wikitext: headings, `''bold''`, `//italic//`, `[[links]]`, `{{transclusions}}`, `<<macros>>`, code blocks, and more)
* Line numbers, active-line highlighting, and an optional code-folding gutter
* Bracket matching and auto-closing brackets/quotes
* Auto-indent, with configurable tab size and tabs-vs-spaces
* Autocomplete: typing `[[` or `{{` suggests tiddler titles, typing `<<` suggests macro/widget names, and JS/CSS/HTML get their own language-aware completions
* Find and replace (`Mod-F` to open the search panel)
* Optional Vim or Emacs keybindings, switchable from the control panel
* Editor chrome matches your active TiddlyWiki palette

Configure all of the above from ''Control panel → Settings → CodeMirror 6''.

!! Keyboard shortcuts

Besides TiddlyWiki's own tiddler-editing shortcuts (save/cancel etc.), the editor itself understands the usual CodeMirror bindings:

|!Shortcut |!Action |
|`Mod-Z` / `Mod-Shift-Z` |Undo / redo |
|`Mod-F` |Open find (and replace) |
|`Mod-G` / `Shift-Mod-G` |Find next / previous |
|`Mod-/` |Toggle line comment |
|`Mod-[` / `Mod-]` |Indent less / more |
|`Mod-Alt-\[` |Fold code at cursor (when the fold gutter is enabled) |
|`Tab` |Accept the current autocomplete suggestion, or indent |

With ''Vim'' or ''Emacs'' keybindings selected in settings, the respective editor's own key bindings take over inside the text area.

!! How it's built

This plugin bundles [[CodeMirror 6|https://codemirror.net/]] (state, view, language, autocomplete, search, and language packages for JavaScript/CSS/HTML/JSON/Markdown, plus `@replit/codemirror-vim`) into a single library tiddler with `esbuild`, and wires it up through TiddlyWiki's standard editor-engine mechanism (`$:/config/EditorTypeMappings/`, an `edit-codemirror6` widget built with `editTextWidgetFactory`, matching how the official `$:/plugins/tiddlywiki/codemirror` plugin integrates CodeMirror 5). The build sources live alongside the plugin folder in `../build`, should you want to change languages, add a highlight tag, or update dependencies and re-bundle.

!! Known limitations

* Settings changes apply to editors opened *after* the change, not to an editor already on screen.
* The wikitext highlighter is a lightweight approximation of TiddlyWiki's grammar, tuned for readability rather than 100% grammatical accuracy.
"},"$:/plugins/samsmith/codemirror6/styles":{"title":"$:/plugins/samsmith/codemirror6/styles","tags":"[[$:/tags/Stylesheet]]","text":"\rules only filteredtranscludeinline transcludeinline macrodef macrocallinline macrocallblock

.cm6tw-wrapper {
	display: block;
	border: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-editor-border>>;
	border-radius: 3px;
	line-height: 1.5;
	font-family: {{$:/themes/tiddlywiki/vanilla/settings/editorfontfamily}};
	font-size: {{$:/themes/tiddlywiki/vanilla/metrics/bodyfontsize}};
	overflow: hidden;
}

.tc-tiddler-frame .tc-tiddler-editor .tc-edit-texteditor,
.tc-tiddler-frame .tc-tiddler-editor .tc-tiddler-preview-preview {
	overflow: auto;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-editor {
	background-color: <<colour tiddler-editor-background>>;
	color: <<colour foreground>>;
	height: 100%;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-editor.cm-focused {
	outline: 2px solid <<colour primary>>;
	outline-offset: -1px;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-scroller {
	font-family: inherit;
	line-height: inherit;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-gutters {
	background-color: <<colour tiddler-editor-background>>;
	color: <<colour foreground>>;
	border-right: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-editor-border>>;
	opacity: 0.6;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-activeLineGutter,
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-activeLine {
	background-color: rgba(127,127,127,0.15);
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-selectionBackground,
.cm6tw-wrapper ::selection {
	background-color: <<colour primary>> !important;
	opacity: 0.35;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-cursor,
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-dropCursor {
	border-left: 2px solid <<colour foreground>>;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-matchingBracket {
	background-color: rgba(133,153,0,0.25);
	font-weight: bold;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-nonmatchingBracket {
	background-color: rgba(220,50,47,0.25);
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-placeholder {
	color: <<colour foreground>>;
	opacity: 0.5;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-foldGutter .cm-gutterElement {
	cursor: pointer;
}

/* Search / replace panel */

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-panels {
	background-color: <<colour tiddler-background>>;
	color: <<colour foreground>>;
	border-top: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-editor-border>>;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-panel input,
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-panel button {
	background-color: <<colour tiddler-editor-background>>;
	color: <<colour foreground>>;
	border: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-editor-border>>;
	border-radius: 3px;
	padding: 2px 4px;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-searchMatch {
	background-color: rgba(243,155,53,0.3);
	outline: 1px solid #f39b35;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-searchMatch-selected {
	background-color: rgba(243,155,53,0.6);
}

/* Autocomplete tooltip */

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-tooltip {
	background-color: <<colour tiddler-background>>;
	border: 1px solid <<colour tiddler-editor-border>>;
	border-radius: 3px;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-tooltip-autocomplete ul li[aria-selected] {
	background-color: <<colour primary>>;
	color: <<colour background>>;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-completionLabel {
	color: inherit;
}

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm-completionMatchedText {
	text-decoration: none;
	font-weight: bold;
	color: <<colour primary>>;
}

/* Syntax token colours (deliberately theme-independent so text stays
   legible on both light and dark tiddler-editor-background choices) */

.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-keyword { color: #cb4b16; font-weight: 600; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-name { color: #839496; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-property { color: #2aa198; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-function { color: #268bd2; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-constant { color: #d33682; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-definition { color: #2aa198; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-type { color: #6c71c4; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-operator { color: #6c71c4; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-link { color: #268bd2; text-decoration: underline; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-tag { color: #93a1a1; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-attribute { color: #b58900; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-string { color: #859900; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-monospace { color: #859900; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-comment { color: #93a1a1; font-style: italic; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-strong { color: inherit; font-weight: bold; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-emphasis { color: inherit; font-style: italic; }
.cm6tw-wrapper .cm6tw-tok-strikethrough { color: inherit; text-decoration: line-through; }
